<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23455" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δάπεδον</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[δᾰ]</span>, τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>level surface,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν τυκτῷ δαπέδῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					4.627
				</span></i>
			; <i>floor of a chamber,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				10.227
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				8.8.16
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				4.952.44
			</span></i> (Epid.); <i>ground, soil,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γῆς ἀρότροις ῥήξας δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Pl.</u>
					515
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόλιος δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					4.200
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Συρίης δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					12.131
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Posidipp.
			</span></i>): abs., <i>ground,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κείμενον ἐν δαπέδῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					11.577
				</span></i>
			: in pl., a ship's <i>decks</i> (fore and aft), <i><span class="en">
				<u>h.Ap.</u>
				416
			</span></i>; but, <i>plain,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				7.34
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Hipp.</u>
				230
			</span></i> (anap.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Βοιωτῶν δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					7.245
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Gaet.
			</span></i>).—Mostly poet.; in later Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Sacr.</u>
				8
			</span></i> alludes to <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4.2
			</span></i>. (From <i>*dṃ-pedo- [dem-, dom-,
				dṃ-,</i>
			= house; expld. by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἶκος,
				ἐρείπιον,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>]; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζάπεδον.</span>)</div>
